---
/** Explain capability and the iterative approach before visitors enter worked examples. */
import CapabilityFoundations from '../components/CapabilityFoundations.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ResourceAbout from '../components/ResourceAbout.astro';
import cycle from '../data/capability-cycle.json';
import diagram from '../assets/capability-cycle.svg?raw';

const steps = cycle.stages.filter(stage => stage.id !== 'refine');
const refinement = cycle.stages.find(stage => stage.id === 'refine')!;
const guide = {
  what: 'A working approach to developing capability: a definition, a seven-step cycle and questions that make each step useful. Refinement continues throughout rather than waiting for a final stage.',
  how: [
    'Start with the capability definition, then follow the pipeline from a challenge through Evaluate and back to Understand. Read the text explanation if the diagram is difficult to view.',
    'Use each step’s decision cue and question on a problem you know. Follow the worked-case or simulation link when you want to examine an example or test a decision.'
  ],
  connection: 'Learning engineering connects human flourishing, learning sciences and systems engineering through evidence-informed iteration. In LENS, this means examining what people can do together with the tools, authority and opportunities that enable action. The cycle makes those assumptions and evidence needs explicit; completing its steps alone does not demonstrate learning or impact.',
  links: [{label: 'Capability Matters: reasoning and evidence', href: '/show-your-work/'}, {label: 'Learning Engineering Commons', href: 'https://lecommons.org/'}]
};
---

<Base title="Approach · Capability Matters" active="approach" description="What capability means, how the seven-step pipeline works, and how evidence drives continuous refinement.">
  <link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href="/capability-pipeline/cycle.css" />
  <link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href="/capability-pipeline/cycle-guide.css" />
  <div class="container approach">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">From challenge to capability</p>
      <h1>Approach</h1>
      <ResourceAbout resource="approach" content={guide} />
      <p class="intro">Bring human flourishing, learning sciences and systems engineering to the same challenge. Understand the work, change the conditions for action, and use evidence to revise decisions. The pipeline offers seven steps with 8. Refine throughout.</p>
    </header>
    <nav class="on-page" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#capability-definition">Capability</a><a href="#foundations">Human, science and system</a><a href="#pipeline">The pipeline</a><a href="#steps">Step explanations</a><a href="#try-it">Explore examples</a>
    </nav>

    <section id="capability-definition" aria-labelledby="capability-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">A working definition</p>
      <h2 id="capability-title">What we mean by capability</h2>
      <p class="definition">The capacity of a person, team, or human-system arrangement to accomplish valued work under stated conditions, with usable opportunities to act.</p>

      <p>We examine output quality, capability, learning, and impact as distinct claims. Each needs evidence that fits the work, its conditions, and the decision being made. A good output alone does not establish that someone learned, can perform independently, or can act in another setting.</p>
      <p class="muted">William Gray-Roncal &amp; James Diamond · Working definition for community discussion, developed in <a href="/show-your-work/">Capability Matters</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <CapabilityFoundations />

    <section id="pipeline" aria-labelledby="pipeline-title">
      <h2 id="pipeline-title">The capability pipeline</h2>
      <p>Start with a challenge. Follow Understand → Map → Design → Build → Instrument → Experiment → Evaluate, then return directly to Understand. Refine any step when evidence changes an assumption; the numbered sequence is a guide to decisions, not a rule to delay feedback.</p>
      <p class="diagram-hint muted">On a narrow screen, scroll the diagram horizontally. The numbered explanations below provide the same sequence in text.</p>
      <figure>
        <div class="diagram-viewport" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Seven-step capability cycle; scroll horizontally on a narrow screen. A text explanation follows."><Fragment set:html={diagram} /></div>
        <figcaption>Challenge → cycle → capability → deployment → challenge. Deployment puts the capability to work through adoption and effective use. Results and evidence return us to the challenge; Refine stays at the center throughout.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="steps" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
      <h2 id="steps-title">What each step asks of us</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        {steps.map(stage => <li id={'step-' + stage.id}>
          <h3>{stage.label}</h3>
          <p><strong>{stage.description}</strong> {stage.why}</p>
          <p><strong>Decision cue:</strong> {stage.decision}</p>
          <p class="question"><strong>Ask:</strong> {stage.question}</p>
        </li>)}
      </ol>
      <aside class="refine" aria-labelledby="refinement-title">
        <h3 id="refinement-title">8. Refine throughout</h3>
        <p>{refinement.description} {refinement.why}</p>
        <p><strong>Decision cue:</strong> {refinement.decision}</p>
        <p><strong>Ask:</strong> {refinement.question}</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="try-it" aria-labelledby="try-title">
      <h2 id="try-title">Explore the approach in practice</h2>
      <p>Worked narratives and a fictional simulation offer different ways to examine these decisions. Each has its own instructions, evidence limits and controls.</p>
      <div class="resources">
        <article><h3><a href="/capability-pipeline/index.html#cases">Explore five worked cases</a></h3><p>Study a narrative, find the turning point, or predict before revealing the explanation. Compare how different system constraints change the decision.</p></article>
        <article><h3><a href="/capability-pipeline/index.html#simulation">Try the branching simulation</a></h3><p>Make decisions in a fictional scenario, inspect outcomes, and compare revised branches. Its probabilities are teaching assumptions, not forecasts.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
      <dialog id="cycle-step-dialog" aria-labelledby="cycle-step-title">
        <form method="dialog"><button class="cycle-close" aria-label="Close step explanation">Close ×</button></form>
        <h2 id="cycle-step-title"></h2><p id="cycle-step-description"></p>
        <h3>Why it matters</h3><p id="cycle-step-why"></p>
        <h3>A decision to make</h3><p id="cycle-step-decision"></p>
        <h3>Ask yourself</h3><p id="cycle-step-question"></p>
      </dialog>
  </div>
  <script is:inline src="/capability-pipeline/teaching.js?v=experiment-20261019"></script>
  <script is:inline src="/capability-pipeline/cycle-guide.js?v=experiment-20261019"></script>
</Base>

<style>
  .approach { --surface: var(--bg); --ink-muted: var(--muted); --font-body: var(--sans); }
  header { padding: 1rem 0; }
  .intro, .definition { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .on-page { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .6rem 1.4rem; margin: 2rem 0; font-family: var(--sans); }
  .on-page a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .2em; }
  section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 2.5rem 0; }
  figure { margin: 2rem 0 0; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--bg); }
  .diagram-viewport { overflow-x: auto; }
  .diagram-hint { font: .9rem/1.6 var(--sans); }
  figcaption { margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--muted); font: .95rem/1.6 var(--sans); }
  .steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1rem; padding: 0; list-style-position: inside; }
  .steps li { padding: 1.25rem; background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; }
  .steps h3 { display: inline; }
  .steps p { margin-top: .7rem; font-size: .95rem; }
  .steps li::marker { font: 600 1.1rem var(--sans); color: var(--accent); }
  .question { color: var(--accent-2); }
  .refine { padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--tint); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-2); }
  .resources { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
  .resources article { padding: 1.4rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; }
  .resources a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .2em; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .resources, .steps { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr); } figure { padding: .5rem; } }
</style>
